### quote-aws-lambda-python manual route testing
###
### This app is server-rendered (Jinja2 + HTMX) rather than a JSON REST API:
### routes return HTML pages/fragments, and most bodies are form-encoded,
### not JSON - same route surface as the quote-k8s-python source app this
### project ports (see ../doc/architecture.md). The one thing that changed
### under the hood: auth is now Cognito ID/refresh-token cookies
### (`id_token`/`refresh_token`) instead of a Flask signed session cookie -
### but from this file's point of view nothing changes. Your HTTP client
### (JetBrains HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client) persists cookies
### automatically within an environment, so once you run a login request
### below, subsequent requests in this file are authenticated as that user -
### no token capture/paste needed.
###
### Select an environment from doc/http-client.env.json before running:
###   deployed  -> the real AWS deployment (API Gateway invoke URL)
###   local-dev -> a local `uv run python wsgi.py` process (see ../doc/deployment.md
###                for the AWS credentials + Cognito/DynamoDB env vars it needs)
###
### The "deployed" baseUrl is whatever `terraform -chdir=infrastructure
### output -raw api_gateway_url` prints for your stack - update
### doc/http-client.env.json if you've destroyed/recreated it since.

### 0.0 Seed demo users (safe to rerun - skips users that already exist)
POST {{baseUrl}}/seed-users

### 0.1 Register a scratch user (for testing)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=scratch-1&email=scratch-1@example.com&password=Password123!&confirm_password=Password123!

### 0.2 Login as the seeded regular user (sets the id_token/refresh_token cookies for later requests)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username={{username-user}}&password={{password-user}}

### 0.3 Login as the seeded admin user (overwrites the cookies above)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username={{username-admin}}&password={{password-admin}}

### ============================================
### PUBLIC / ANONYMOUS QUOTE BROWSING
### ============================================

### 1. Main quote view (full HTML page)
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### 2. New quote, anonymous (random, excluding already-seen ids)
POST {{baseUrl}}/quote/new
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

excluded_ids=1,2,3

### ============================================
### AUTHENTICATED QUOTE BROWSING (run 0.2 or 0.3 first)
### ============================================

### 3. New quote, authenticated (sequential - advances user_progress)
POST {{baseUrl}}/quote/new

### 4. Re-fetch a specific quote by id (Previous/Next/First/Last; does not advance progress)
GET {{baseUrl}}/quote/1

### 5. Like quote 1 (idempotent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/quote/1/like

### 6. Unlike quote 1 (idempotent)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/quote/1/unlike

### 7. Favourites quick-view strip fragment
GET {{baseUrl}}/favourites/strip

### ============================================
### MANAGE FAVOURITES
### ============================================

### 8. Favourites table fragment
GET {{baseUrl}}/favourites/table

### 9. Like a couple of quotes to have something to reorder
POST {{baseUrl}}/quote/2/like

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/quote/3/like

### 10. Move quote 3 up one position
PUT {{baseUrl}}/favourites/3/reorder
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

direction=up

### 11. Remove quote 2 from favourites
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/favourites/2

### ============================================
### MANAGE VIEWED QUOTES
### ============================================

### 12. Viewed Quotes page (full HTML page)
GET {{baseUrl}}/manage/viewed

### 13. Toggle like on quote 1 from the viewed-quotes row
POST {{baseUrl}}/viewed/1/toggle-like

### 14. Delete all viewed + liked quotes and reset progress to 0
POST {{baseUrl}}/viewed/delete-all

### ============================================
### ADMIN: USER MANAGEMENT (run 0.3 first - ADMIN role required)
### ============================================

### 15. Users table fragment
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/table

### 16. Grant ADMIN role to the scratch user (idempotent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/scratch-1/roles/ADMIN

### 17. Revoke ADMIN role from the scratch user
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/scratch-1/roles/ADMIN

### 18. Delete the scratch user (cascades likes/progress + removes the Cognito identity)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/scratch-1

### 19. Self-protection: admin cannot revoke their own ADMIN role
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/{{username-admin}}/roles/ADMIN

### 20. Self-protection: admin cannot delete their own account
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/{{username-admin}}

### ============================================
### ADMIN: QUOTE MANAGEMENT (ADMIN role required)
### ============================================

### 21. Paginated/sorted/searched quotes table
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/quotes/table?page=1&page_size=10&sort_by=id&sort_order=asc

### 22. Search by quote text and author
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/quotes/table?q=life&author=carnegie&page=1

### 23. Sort by likes (descending-only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/quotes/table?sort_by=likes&sort_order=desc

### 24. Force-fetch more quotes from ZenQuotes (dedup by text+author)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/quotes/fetch-zen

### ============================================
### PERMISSION / ERROR TESTING
### ============================================

### 25. Login as the regular (non-admin) user, then rerun the admin requests above -
###     they should return 403 with an inline error toast fragment.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username={{username-user}}&password={{password-user}}

### 26. Non-admin hitting an admin route -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/table

### 27. Log out (clears the id_token/refresh_token cookies)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout

### 28. Login-required route without a session -> 302 redirect to /login
###     (a real browser follows this automatically; an HTMX request instead
###     gets an HX-Redirect response header - see app/auth/decorators.py)
GET {{baseUrl}}/profile

### 29. Login with a wrong password -> 401 with an inline error fragment
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username={{username-user}}&password=not-the-right-password

### 30. Healthz (liveness probe target - a cheap DynamoDB GetItem, see app/health/routes.py)
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz
